WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:05.670 align:start position:0%
 
a little while back  i misinterpreted something that youtube  had put  as a suggestion about how we might reach  fans and subscribers as a new future  that they had rolled  out so as you can see here i wrote  trying out this new suggested feature in  youtube  caption contest youtube was just telling  us you should run  caption contests so i did that with this  image from one of my intro to philosophy  classes  at marist college back in about 2011  and there were a number of interesting  captions for it  and queries and questions and comments  so two that came up right away lenny  penny wrote i want to know the context  for this picture  and jeffrey bailey asked where was this  at  so of course the answer to that is it  was at marist college  in poughkeepsie new york i had recently  moved up there in 2011 leaving my  position  as an assistant professor up for early  tenure and promotion  i moved up to the hudson valley to be  with my at that point  uh fiance now now wife andy  and i began teaching as an adjunct at  marist college  where i got to teach intro to philosophy  and ethics classes and  so you know aristotle was one of the  people i wanted to teach in intro to  philosophy and we did the metaphysics  book one  so that talks about different causes and  you notice that  on the screen behind me or rather the  chalkboard behind me there is a diagram  about  the different four causes efficient  final formal and material and i was  using props that day  to demonstrate it so i brought in my  dad's old banjo been my banjo for  really decades now and i thought this  would be a useful  way to convey things and students really  responded to it they always love when  you bring in  any sort of you know unusual things and  a banjo is probably better for that than  a guitar i also brought in a recorder  that day as well and i think i might  have used a sandwich as another example  so that's what was going on you can see  me here  basically walking them through things  about the banjo and its causality using  aristotle's ideas so i said  caption this and people did the first  three captions were really about  you might say jokey things that have to  do with with  music so the first one the banjo at the  gates of dawn  not really about banjos as such that's a  reference to  pink floyd's piper at the gates of dawn  record but i thought that was kind of  funny  then somebody had something that was  specifically about banjo's  foggy aristotelian breakdown i think  it's foggy mountain breakdown it's kind  of an old-timey banjo  song and then we have so is reading  foucault  down on the bayou foucault of course is  a french philosopher and historian  and banjos are associated with uh among  other things  um louisiana and so that that makes a  bit of sense  then there were some other good comments  as well  uh probably only fellow banjo players  will get this one but how about  philosophizing with a  claw hammer so you know who is the  philosopher with the hammer that would  be friedrich nietzsche  and claw hammer is a particular style of  playing with the banjo that i actually  do myself use from time to time  the next one i kind of got a kick out of  this one i can just play this banjo  until you're all ready to settle down  and pay attention i can play it all day  your choice there's this is a bit of a  side note but there's always this  notion that like banjo playing is  somehow  you know like bagpipes it's not for  everybody and  maybe it would be a punishment to play  it in a class or  something like that the next one uh  dialectic banjos aristotelian  deliverance from andoxa they managed to  really pack a lot of  ideas into that one so instead of  dueling banjos  dialectic banjos okay makes sense with  aristotle since he does talk about  the dialectic uh process  and dialectics involve and doxa these  are  common ideas about things and of course  you know deliverance is the movie  where dueling banjos is a a major part  of the soundtrack  the next one pov you try to get into  philosophy by reading  kant and end up losing your mind i  thought that was kind of funny it  doesn't really have much to do with the  banjo first say  but i thought that uh yeah you know  reading kant you you could lose your  mind and maybe then you bring a banjo to  class  uh the next one wittgenstein ending  philosophy  circa 1921  colorized the idea would be that very  improbable that that wittgenstein would  do so with the banjo which  was actually an instrument used in bands  at that time but  you know i don't know that wittgenstein  had any connections to  to music per se but i might be wrong  about that  and then the last two are particularly  good so i really like this one yeah  that's how i beat the devil in a banjo  contest when he came up here and tried  to give  get me to give up my book collection so  you know there's the  old story about the devil going down to  georgia now that has to do with a fiddle  not a banjo but it's still sort of a you  know  country instrument and uh you know  beating the devil in a banjo contest i  guess would be quite a thing to do  and last and definitely not least we  have  from virginia charlotte a little poem  uh someday we'll find it the metaphysics  four causes the matter form  agent and end all of its un under its  spell we know  aristotle is magic  and uh i imagine this is supposed to be  a song set to music so  kind of a nice response there as well so  those are  the best of the responses that i got  from this particular caption contest i  thought i would  share the results of my  mistake with you and some of you might  get a  kick out of it you know i do i'll put a  link  below to a video where i'm actually  discussing this banjo in question you  can click  see more and also put a link to the  aristotle lecture  as such from this this particular class  so you can click on that as well but  i'll do more of these caption contests  in the future if people are  interested in them i'll find some other  good images maybe from classes or maybe  from some  other things and we'll we'll see what  people come up with and then i'll make  some  videos about them  you

